    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5459956/27-06-tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-mathematics": {
      "title": "27-06 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "27-06 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mathematics Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-06 Department College of the Sciences & Mathematics Division Mathematics Opening Date 10/08/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Department of Mathematics invites applicants for a Full-time, Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor of Mathematics position. The position begins in August 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The mission of the College of the Sciences and Mathematics, home of the Department of Mathematics, is to prepare the students of West Chester University to be informed citizens and successful professionals, through our academic programs and co-curricular experiences in the computational, mathematical, natural, and social sciences, as well as engineering. The Department’s faculty hold advanced degrees from major universities with gained recognition both nationally and internationally in research and teaching. The faculty members serve as both instructors and scholarly practitioners dedicated to student success. Learn more about the Department of Mathematics . The faculty position involves teaching undergraduate and/or graduate level courses that may be offered in in-person, online, and/or hybrid modalities depending on departmental needs including evening schedules. The ideal candidate will use innovative teaching skills and demonstrate strong attention to the learning and teaching needs of the department’s students. Their experience, substantive specialization, and pedagogical training will serve to strengthen the department's mission and vision. The faculty will collaborate with other departmental and college faculty & staff to ensure student success. Responsibilities include: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate, including electives, principles, and intermediate level courses in Mathematics via approved modalities. Additional courses may be assigned based on area of specialization depending on department needs. Engage in scholarly activities such as research, presentations, publications and grant writing Mentor and advise students Serve the Department and University community through participation in various committees Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field. ABD may be considered – Doctoral dissertation must be successfully completed on or before August 2027; and Record of scholarship and research experience in scientific computing, operations research, mathematical modeling, or applied analysis; and Demonstrated experience teaching at a collegiate level Preferred Qualifications Experience leading the development of undergraduate or graduate research initiatives; and/or Experience contributing to the development of Departmental programs; and/or Experience teaching courses in diverse areas of mathematics - includes undergraduate & graduate majors, and general education courses; and/or Experience authoring or co-authoring grant or attracting external research funding Experience teaching in various modalities, including online synchronous, online asynchronous, or a hybrid format Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications began in October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. In accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, teaching demonstration, and research presentation to be considered a finalist. The University's ability to sponsor or extend employment-based immigration benefits is subject to the availability of institutional resources and compliance with all applicable laws and regulations. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Cover letter – address the minimum and (if any) preferred qualifications Curriculum vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness Statement of teaching philosophy Statement of research interest – include how you will include undergraduate in research. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required at a later date) List of three (3) references (Include name, email address, and phone number for each reference). Letter of recommendation will be solicited electronically. Service Statement (see below). This will be requested at a later date. West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Do you possess a Ph.D. in Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field? ABD may be considered – Doctoral dissertation must be completed on or before August 2027. Yes No 02 Do you have a record of scholarship and research experience in scientific computing, operations research, mathematical modeling, or applied analysis? Yes No 03 Have you demonstrated experience teaching at a collegiate level? Yes No 04 Have you uploaded the following: • Cover letter – address the minimum and (if any) preferred qualifications • Curriculum vitae • Evidence of teaching effectiveness • Statement of teaching philosophy • Statement of research interest – include how you will include undergraduate in research. • Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required at a later date) • List of three (3) references (Include name, email address, and phone number for each reference). Letter of recommendation will be solicited electronically. Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5499880/27-48-administrative-assistant-aa1-psychology-department": {
      "title": "27-48 Administrative Assistant (AA1) – Psychology Department",
      "description": "27-48 Administrative Assistant (AA1) – Psychology Department Salary $49,819.00 Annually Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-48 Department College of the Sciences & Mathematics Division Psychology Opening Date 09/30/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Join a vibrant campus community whose excellence is reflected in its diversity and student success. West Chester University of Pennsylvania’s Psychology Department in the College of Sciences and Mathematics invites applicants for the position of Administrative Assistant. The shift for the position is Monday to Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. West Chester University, a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU proudly offers a positive and purposeful work environment; comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance along with many wellness programs; a commitment to work-life balance including generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays; and a University mission to support employee personal and professional growth including a tuition waiver for self and family members, training and development, and advancement opportunities. The Psychology Department seeks to advance the discipline of Psychology as an area of scholarly, professional, and scientific endeavors in a diverse and inclusive environment. The department focus is to provide a high quality, liberal-arts education wherein students and faculty members exchange ideas stemming from a variety of viewpoints in an environment of mutual respect, collaboration, and equity. As a key psychology department team contributor, the administrative assistant provides excellent customer service and administrative support to students, the department chairperson, assistant chairperson and faculty, and the student success coordinator in a fast-paced environment. The ideal candidate will demonstrate excellent customer service skills; strong organizational skills; the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced and high-volume environment; technology proficiency; the ability to effectively communicate in writing and verbally and interact dynamically with a variety of constituents. Responsibilities include: Receive and announce visitors Respond to walk-in inquiries Answering calls Maintain department email accounts and respond to routine inquiries Respond to general student information requests about course registration process and how to contact faculty and field experience courses Assist with the building of Psychology department courses in Ram Portal; make changes to department course schedule as needed and as directed by the chairperson Support enrollment management efforts using Ram Portal and Navigate Process and assist with faculty purchasing requests and reimbursements for supplies and travel expenses Assist with scheduling of first year students and new transfer students Assist with faculty search process Maintain department office files Maintain department website, bulletin boards and signage Maintain department SharePoint, Teams and social media websites Maintain department mailroom, including mail distribution, copier, printers, fax machine and supply cabinet Oversee office supply inventory and ordering Provide scheduling and calendar support for the department chairperson Manage usage of Wayne Hall classrooms and general use laboratories Assist with psychology faculty requests for conference room scheduling, computer lab scheduling, etc. Oversee department laptop, equipment, book, and video checkout processes General department budget administration, monitor and process multiple department purchase cards including reconciliation of monthly statements, purchasing requisitions and transfer of funds Process department work orders and equipment maintenance Support department events (new student orientation, learning community events, etc.) Seek out training to maintain and enhance software skills and learn new systems as they are adopted by department and the university Perform other related duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Such training may have been gained through graduation from a four-year college OR university or any equivalent combination of experience and training. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office including Outlook, Teams, and Excel Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Some knowledge of the principles and practices of public administration. Some knowledge of the principles of governmental accounting, statistics, and public personnel administration. Some knowledge of the sources of information, methods, and techniques used in administrative research. Ability to carry out, with some supervision, staff assignments requiring the organization of material and development of procedures. Ability to conduct studies and analyze contributing to the development of sound operational procedures. Ability to speak and write effectively. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with administrative officials, other employees, and the general public. Preferred Qualifications Associates degree or higher Experience in an administrative or receptionist role Customer service experience Experience in higher education or student support Experience with higher education software systems and enterprise technologies, including Slate, PeopleSoft, Banner, Navigate, D2L, OnBase, SAP, and Business Intelligence (BI) tools. Excellent written communication skills Special Instructions Salary and benefits are dictated by the American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees (AFSCME) collective bargaining agreement. Candidates should apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Required Documents for Consideration: Resume Cover letter A list of three references with contact information Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the interview process to be considered as a finalist. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all pre-employment background checks. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical benefit plans and can choose between two PPO plans or an HMO plan. Supplemental dental, vision, hearing and prescription coverage is also offered to employees. The Get Healthy Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is American Federation of State, County, and Municipal Employees (AFSCME). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
