    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5500784/27-50-associate-registrar-for-academic-technology-business-analyst-manager-180": {
      "title": "27-50 Associate Registrar for Academic Technology/Business Analyst (Manager 180)",
      "description": "27-50 Associate Registrar for Academic Technology/Business Analyst (Manager 180) Salary $86,565.00 Annually Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-50 Department Academic Affairs Division Registrar's Office Opening Date 09/30/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Office of the Registrar invites applicants for the position of Associate Registrar for Academic Technology/Business Analyst (Manager 180). West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . WCU proudly offers a positive and purposeful work environment; comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance along with many wellness programs; a commitment to work-life balance including generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays; and a University mission to support employee personal and professional growth including a tuition waiver for self and family members, training and development, and advancement opportunities. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President & University Registrar, the Associate Registrar for Academic Technology/Business Analyst provides guidance and leadership on the technical aspects of student record management including requirement gathering, testing, and training. The Associate Registrar will set up Banner tables and forms for the term, perform records maintenance, testing and validation of new reports, workflows, and functionality, and optimization of the Ellucian Banner student information systems (SIS). The Associate Registrar collaborates to develop and support new initiatives to improve system efficiency, reporting, and staffing training. This position also provides project management for both current projects as well as updates and monitors the on-going office production calendar. The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong leadership possessing functional expertise and excellent project management skills. This person will be highly collaborative, intently communicative, and work independently in a fast-paced, high volume, deadline driven, and team orientated environment. The candidate will leverage their experience and expertise to the organization’s processes and architecture whilst ensuring adherence to established industry standards and national best practices across all functions. Responsibilities include: Collaborate with the Office of the Registrar, Academic and Enterprise Systems, and other campus partners to develop, improve, and streamline registration and student records processes in registrar systems, including Banner, Argos, DegreeWorks, and OnBase Serve as a functional lead for the Banner Student Information System (SIS), especially for new functionality and system testing and validation Track, schedule, and plan for system upgrades, including collaboration with staff on testing and changes Lead Registrar reporting spec development and testing (Argos) Support the degree audit (DegreeWorks) as needed Manage and improve the Office of the Registrar production calendar and monitor deliverables and deadlines Lead preparation timeline for each registration cycle and support system set up Assist in the planning and development of staff training, documentation, development opportunities, and retreats Proactively monitor student record data and identify gaps in business processes Coordinate with other offices including Admissions, Financial Aid, Bursar, and The Graduate School to support system needs Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Two years of system project management experience Technical and/or Functional experience using student information systems/applications (example: Banner, Argos, DegreeWorks, ProcessMaker, OnBase, 25Live, Parchment, and CourseLeaf) Experience establishing report specification(s) and testing/validation standards Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree; and/or Two years of higher education, enrollment, or Registrar's Office experience; and/or Demonstrated knowledge of Registrar practices and procedures; and/or Technical/Functional experiencing working with Ellucian Banner application; and/or Experience developing reports; and/or Experience creating systems documentation; and/or Experience creating training materials; and/or Experience using JIRA project management applications; and/or Experience coordinating and conducting systems testing; and/or Experience working collaboratively across functional teams Special Instructions There is the possibility of working remotely occasionally subject to departmental operations. The salary for this position is $86,565. Excellent benefits package including undergraduate tuition fee waiver for self and dependents. Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered an applicant for the position, please submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae/Resume List of three references with contact information (Include position title, phone number, and email address). To be considered a finalist, applicants must successfully complete the application and interview process. Due to the nature of this position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Nonrepresented Employees (Managers). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Do you have a Bachelor’s Degree? Yes No 02 Do you have experience with Banner Ellucian SIS? Yes No 03 Do you have at least two years of higher education, enrollment, or Registrar's Office experience? Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
