    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5511398/27-44-admissions-processing-coordinator-management-technician-graduate-school": {
      "title": "27-44 Admissions Processing Coordinator (Management Technician) – Graduate School",
      "description": "27-44 Admissions Processing Coordinator (Management Technician) – Graduate School Salary $49,819.00 Annually Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-44 Department Academic Affairs Division Graduate School Opening Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date 10/30/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Position Summary Join a vibrant campus community whose excellence is reflected in its diversity and student success. West Chester University of Pennsylvania Graduate School invites applicants for the position of Admissions Processing Coordinator. The shift for the position is Monday to Friday, 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. West Chester University, a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. Reporting to the Associate Director of Graduate School Admissions and Outreach, the selected candidate will work on processing graduate school application documents and correspondence, scanning applicant credentials into the document imaging system and verifying data by utilizing queries in the admissions CRM. The ideal candidate will demonstrate excellent customer service skills; strong organizational skills; the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced and high-volume environment; technology proficiency; and the ability to effectively communicate in writing and verbally and interact dynamically with a variety of constituents. Responsibilities include : Serve as first point of contact for phone calls and in person walk-ins from applicants and prospective students, referring them to staff as appropriate; assist with phone calls as needed by providing courteous telephone service to all customers; document details of all calls and interactions Participate in Graduate School events including commencement preparations and ceremonies, open houses and information sessions and new student orientations Receive and process incoming transcripts, test scores, letters of recommendation and other application materials Verify completeness and accuracy of submitted materials by identifying and resolving discrepancies (mismatched names, missing pages, fraudulent scans, unofficial vs. official documents, etc.) Match and attach materials to the correct applicant record in Slate and ensure the applicant checklist is accurate Triage the Graduate Admissions email inbox to appropriate staff members Investigate and resolve complex applicant issues by cross-referencing multiple systems and sources (e.g., Banner, OnBase, Slate, score report portals, email correspondence) to locate missing transcripts or other materials Maintain up-to-date processing documentation and standard operating procedures for Slate workflows Coordinate with external credential services (e.g., WES, ECE) for access and applicant materials as needed Maintain strict confidentiality of student records in compliance with FERPA and institutional data policies Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Three years of advanced clerical or para-professional work which included collection, recording, compilation, and presentation of office management or program related information OR Any equivalent combination of experience and training. An associate’s degree may be substituted for two years of required experience. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office including Outlook, Word, and Excel Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of the basic principles and practices and the respective standards of measurement applied within a management discipline. Knowledge of modern office practices and equipment. Knowledge of basic PC hardware and standard software. Ability to use a PC to collect, compile, and assemble data and reports for use in the conduct of studies. Ability to analyze varied data by applying the information against interpretive standards in the formulation of recommended action. Ability to perform detailed work involving written information by preparing reports of finding according to the appropriate standards of content, clarity, grammar, and format. Ability to identify problems and recognize appropriate solutions as a result of the analysis of data. Ability to communicate effectively with employees, programs officials, job applicants and the public by relating the purpose of the contact and collecting all the necessary information required for the analysis. Ability to apply and adapt established procedures to the preparation and formulation of study findings. Ability to learn the basic principles and practices of public administration. Ability to read, write, and communicate orally in English. Ability to develop and maintain effective working relationships with associates in the performance of work. Preferred Qualifications Customer service experience Experience using enterprise resource planning platforms such as Slate, OnBase and Banner Special Instructions Salary and benefits are dictated by the American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees (AFSCME) collective bargaining agreement. Candidates should apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . To be considered for the position, upload the following required documentation to the application: Resume List of three references with contact information Incomplete applications will not be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Due to the nature of the position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants must successfully complete the interview process to be considered as a finalist. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all pre-employment background checks. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical benefit plans and can choose between two PPO plans or an HMO plan. Supplemental dental, vision, hearing and prescription coverage is also offered to employees. The Get Healthy Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is American Federation of State, County, and Municipal Employees (AFSCME). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5515050/27-56-carpentry-shop-maintenance-repairman-two-vacancies-mr2-facilities-divi": {
      "title": "27-56 Carpentry Shop Maintenance Repairman (Two Vacancies, MR2) - Facilities Division",
      "description": "27-56 Carpentry Shop Maintenance Repairman (Two Vacancies, MR2) - Facilities Division Salary $44,147.00 Annually Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-56 Department Finance & Administration Division Carpenter Shop Opening Date 10/13/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant campus community whose excellence is reflected in its diversity and student success. West Chester University of Pennsylvania’s Facilities Division invites applicants for the two vacant positions of Carpentry Shop Maintenance Repairman. The shift for the position is Monday to Friday 6:00 a.m. – 2:00 p.m. West Chester University, a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU proudly offers a positive and purposeful work environment; comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance along with many wellness programs; a commitment to work-life balance including generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays; and a University mission to support employee personal and professional growth including a tuition waiver for self and family members, training and development, and advancement opportunities. Under the supervision of the Carpenter Shop Foreman, perform journey level work in the carpentry trade. Participate in all interior/exterior carpentry work performed on campus. This position has a high focus on all aspects of carpentry and will also assist with roofing and masonry work as needed. Works with other members of the carpenter shop to complete tasks from start to finish with a high level of quality and workmanship. The selected candidate must have the ability to lift 80 lbs. and work from heights using lifts, bucket truck, ladders & scaffolding, both interior and exterior. Must have familiarity to operate and maintain carpentry tools, woodworking machinery, lifts, and power equipment safely and efficiently. Responsibilities include: Ensure all carpentry work is in adherence to specifications and standards set by the University, Federal, State, and local municipalities Read and interpret blueprints, construction drawings, specifications, and technical manuals Track labor, materials, and time requirements for assigned work orders Maintain records of completed work orders, preventative maintenance, inspections, and material usage Utilize a variety of carpentry and masonry hand tools, portable and stationary power tools, and leveling and measuring instruments Repair, countertops, cabinets, benches, partitions, floors, doors, building framing and a variety of finish trim work Assist with installing, repairing, and maintaining doors, frames, windows, cabinetry, furniture, partitions, ceilings, and flooring systems Support minor bathroom, office, kitchen classroom renovations Layout and install various types of flooring i.e. carpet, tile, wood Respond to emergency maintenance calls involving structural damage, security concerns, or facility repairs Coordinate work activities with facilities management staff, contractors, electricians, plumbers, painters, and HVAC personnel Assist with event setups, classroom modifications, and campus improvement projects Assist with repairs of spouting, metal roofing parts, and flashing for buildings. Supports maintenance of roofing systems made up of asphalt, rubber, shingles, tile and slates. Cleans, maintains, repairs and installs rainspouts, eave boxes, gutters and roof drains Construct forms, mix and pour concrete, and apply different finishes in accordance with all building standards and codes Assist mason with minor masonry work on buildings i.e. pointing, stone/block/stucco repair Perform other duties as assigned This position is deemed \"essential\" and must remain or report to work during partial or full day closings of the University due to hazardous road conditions, emergency circumstances or for other reasons. The ability to work overtime when needed is also required. Minimum Qualifications Four years of experience in building and plant maintenance work, which has involved at least two of the building, electrical, or mechanical trades OR Two years of experience as a Maintenance Repairman 1; OR Any equivalent combination of experience and training Valid Driver's License Required Knowledge Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of the methods, materials, tools, and practices used in at least two of the building, electrical, or mechanical trades. Knowledge of the occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trades involved. Ability to care for and use the tools and equipment utilized in the trades involved. Ability to detect defects in equipment and to make proper repairs or adjustments. Ability to lead a small group of semi-skilled workers. Ability to interpret and work from pencil sketches and diagrams. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to operate and/or utilize basic lawn care and snow removal equipment. Ability to lift and move heavy objects and to work under adverse weather conditions. Preferred Qualifications Completion of a trade school carpentry program Minimum of three years’ experience working for a general contractor Special Instructions Salary and benefits are dictated by the American Federation of State, County and Municipal Employees (AFSCME) collective bargaining agreement. Candidates must apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Due to the nature of this position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. Applicants must successfully complete the interview process to be considered as a finalist. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical benefit plans and can choose between two PPO plans or an HMO plan. Supplemental dental, vision, hearing and prescription coverage is also offered to employees. The Get Healthy Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is American Federation of State, County, and Municipal Employees (AFSCME). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Have you attended trade school for carpentry? Yes No 02 Have you worked for a minimum of three years for a general contractor? Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5515948/27-47-head-softball-coach-athletics-department": {
      "title": "27-47 Head Softball Coach – Athletics Department",
      "description": "27-47 Head Softball Coach – Athletics Department Salary See Position Description Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-47 Department University Affairs Division Athletics Opening Date 10/14/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Department of Athletics invites applicants for a Head Softball Coach position. This a Full-Time, salaried, 12-month position with benefits. West Chester University is an NCAA Division II member of the highly competitive Pennsylvania State Athletic Conference (PSAC). The Department of Athletics prepares our student athletes for life-long success by providing opportunities for them to excel in the classroom, in competition and in the community. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. Learn more about WCU’s Department of Athletics . The Head Softball Coach is responsible for all aspects of administering and operating an NCAA Division II program. The incumbent will supervise full-time and volunteer assistant coaches, recruit qualified prospective student-athletes, run summer camps and clinics as well as other fundraising events, and handle the administrative functions of the program. This position requires regular afternoon, evening, and weekend availability, including travel with the team to all competitions. The ideal candidate will be responsible for fulfilling all duties associated with successful coaching at the college level and will demonstrate excellent communication, organizational, and leadership skills to be a positive role model and representative of the university. This person will manage multiple priorities and assignments. This Softball Head Coach will collaborate with other departmental staff to ensure student success. Responsibilities include: Coaching and Program Leadership Plan and conduct all practices, conditioning, and competition for the varsity softball program. Develop and implement offensive, defensive, and pitching strategies suited to PSAC and NCAA Division II competition. Prepare the competitive schedule, including fall and non-traditional segments, within NCAA and PSAC limits. Hire, train, supervise, and evaluate assistant coaches, graduate assistants, and volunteer staff. Recruiting Identify, evaluate, and recruit prospective student-athletes who fit WCU academically, athletically, and socially. Manage recruiting within the program's scholarship allocation and the department's financial aid guidelines. Build and maintain relationships with high school, travel ball, and junior college coaches. Student-Athlete Development and Welfare Monitor academic progress and support timely graduation in partnership with academic support staff. Promote student-athlete health, safety, and well-being in coordination with sports medicine and strength and conditioning staff. Foster a positive team culture rooted in accountability, respect, and inclusion. Encourage participation in community service, leadership programming, and the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC). Compliance Know and follow all NCAA, PSAC, and University rules and policies; ensure staff and student-athletes do the same. Complete required compliance education, recruiting documentation, and certifications on time. Administration, Budget, and Facilities Manage the program's operating budget, travel, and equipment responsibly and within university procedures. Coordinate facility scheduling, field maintenance needs, and game-day operations with athletics staff. Fundraising, Alumni, and Community Relations Partner with athletics development on fundraising, including the Golden Ram Athletic Fund and program-specific giving. Engage alumni, parents, and the community through events, camps, and clinics. Represent the program professionally with media, campus partners, and the public. Other Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Five years of previous high school and/or two years of college coaching experience in softball Knowledge of and conformity to NCAA rules Demonstrated ability to effectively communicate in writing & verbally, and present dynamically to a variety of constituents Possess a valid driver’s license and ability to travel with the team, including driving team vans (15-passenger van) Ability to work evenings, weekends, and a flexible schedule during the academic year Preferred Qualifications Head coaching or FT assistant experience at the NCAA level; and/or Working knowledge of PSAC, Institutional rules, and affiliated student related governance and compliance practices; and/or Familiarity with the PSAC and the Mid-Atlantic recruiting landscape. Record of team academic achievement (team GPA, Academic Success Rate); and/or Experience with fundraising, alumni engagement, and running camps and clinics; and/or Proficiency with video analysis, performance analytics, and recruiting and roster management software Special Instructions The salary for this position is commensurate with experience and APSCUF Coaches’ Union collective bargaining agreement. Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered an applicant for the position, please submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae/Resume List of three references with contact information (Include position title, phone number, and email address). To be considered a finalist, applicants must successfully complete the application and interview process. Due to the nature of this position, employment visa sponsorship is not available. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5479142/27-36-tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-medical-surgical-nursing": {
      "title": "27-36 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Medical-Surgical Nursing",
      "description": "27-36 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Medical-Surgical Nursing Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-36 Department College of Health Sciences Division Nursing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus community whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The School of Nursing invites applicants for a Full-time, 9-month, Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor of Medical-Surgical Nursing. We seek an enthusiastic nurse educator with expertise in adult health and medical-surgical nursing to contribute primarily to our undergraduate prelicensure nursing programs. The position begins in August 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The mission of the School of Nursing, part of the College of Health Sciences, is to provide high-quality undergraduate and graduate nursing education to students from diverse populations. The School of Nursing is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and approved by the State Board of Nursing of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Faculty balance excellence in teaching with active scholarship and service. Learn more about the School of Nursing . The faculty position involves teaching undergraduate nursing courses that may be offered through in-person and/or distance education modalities, with a primary focus on the nursing care of adults experiencing acute and chronic health conditions. Teaching responsibilities may include didactic, clinical, simulation, laboratory, and other experiential learning experiences. The successful candidate will contribute to the design, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the undergraduate nursing curriculum and demonstrate attention to the learning and teaching needs of students. The faculty member will collaborate with other School of Nursing and College faculty and staff to promote student success. The typical course load involves teaching twelve credits per semester. The appointment will include working with affiliated agencies and clinical partners and will necessitate satisfying contractual obligations such as health requirements, physical guidelines, clinical hours, codes of conduct, and other agency-specific requirements. Responsibilities include : Contribute to the instructional program in the Traditional BSN and accelerated second-degree prelicensure nursing programs. Provide didactic and clinical teaching in medical-surgical/adult health nursing. Facilitate learning in classroom, clinical, simulation, laboratory, and other experiential learning environments. Incorporate evidence-based teaching strategies that promote clinical judgment, clinical reasoning, patient safety, and readiness for professional nursing practice. Participate in the development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the undergraduate nursing curriculum. Collaborate with clinical partners and affiliated agencies to provide high-quality clinical learning experiences. Demonstrate a commitment to student success through teaching, advising, mentoring, and academic support. Maintain an active research and scholarly agenda. Demonstrate continuing scholarly growth compatible with the teacher-scholar model. Serve the School of Nursing, College of Health Sciences, University, profession, and community through participation in committees and other service activities. Advise and mentor students. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing or a closely related field Evidence of matriculation and significant progress in a doctoral program of study, with the expectation that the terminal degree will be completed by the end of the second year of appointment Eligibility for Registered Nurse licensure in Pennsylvania, with verification of licensure required at the start of employment At least two years of professional nursing experience in adult health and/or medical-surgical nursing practice Ability to meet the requirements of contractual affiliation agreements with clinical partners. These requirements may include, but are not limited to, health requirements, physical guidelines, clinical hours, background clearances, and codes of conduct. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate in Nursing or a closely related field; and/or Didactic teaching experience; and/or Experience teaching medical-surgical/adult health nursing courses or curriculum; and/or Recent (within 5 years) clinical experience in adult health, acute care, or medical-surgical nursing. Experience teaching undergraduate prelicensure nursing students; and/or Experience with simulation, clinical judgment activities, or other innovative experiential learning strategies; and/or Experience using learning management systems such as D2L, Canvas, Blackboard, or similar platforms. This includes using the educational technology in mixed modalities (face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online); and/or Evidence of scholarly activity and/or potential for development of a sustained program of scholarship; and/or Experience teaching, advising, or mentoring students from diverse backgrounds. Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, research presentation, and teaching demonstration to be considered as a finalist. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial transcript(s); official transcripts will be required for final consideration List of three (3) references. Provide name, email address, and phone number for each reference. Service Statement (see below): West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Do you have a Master's degree in Nursing or a closely related field? Yes No 02 Do you have evidence of matriculation and significant progress in a doctoral program of study, with the expectation that the terminal degree will be completed by the end of the second year of appointment? Yes No 03 Do you have eligibility for Registered Nurse licensure in Pennsylvania, with verification of licensure required at the start of employment? Yes No 04 Do you have at least two years of professional nursing experience in adult health and/or medical-surgical nursing practice? Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5479157/27-37-tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-psychiatric-mental-health-nursing": {
      "title": "27-37 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing",
      "description": "27-37 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-37 Department College of Health Sciences Division Nursing Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus community whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The School of Nursing invites applicants for a Full-time, 9-month, Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor of Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing. We seek an enthusiastic nurse educator with expertise in psychiatric-mental health and behavioral health nursing to contribute primarily to our undergraduate prelicensure nursing programs. This position is specifically focused on undergraduate/prelicensure psychiatric-mental health nursing education and is not an advanced practice or nurse practitioner faculty position. The position begins in August 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The mission of the School of Nursing, part of the College of Health Sciences, is to provide high-quality undergraduate and graduate nursing education to students from diverse populations. The School of Nursing is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and approved by the State Board of Nursing of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Faculty balance excellence in teaching with active scholarship and service. Learn more about the School of Nursing . The successful candidate will contribute to the design, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the undergraduate nursing curriculum and demonstrate attention to the learning and teaching needs of students. The faculty member will collaborate with School of Nursing and College faculty and staff, as well as clinical and community partners, to promote student success. The appointment will include working with affiliated agencies and clinical partners and will necessitate satisfying contractual obligations such as health requirements, physical guidelines, clinical hours, codes of conduct, and other agency-specific requirements. The typical course load involves teaching twelve credits per semester. Responsibilities include : Contribute to the instructional program in the Traditional BSN and accelerated second-degree prelicensure nursing programs. Provide didactic and clinical teaching in undergraduate psychiatric-mental health nursing. Facilitate learning in classroom, clinical, simulation, community-based, and other experiential learning environments. Prepare students to apply therapeutic communication, clinical judgment, evidence-based practice, patient safety, trauma-informed approaches, and person-centered care when caring for individuals experiencing mental and behavioral health conditions. Participate in the development, implementation, evaluation, and continuous improvement of the undergraduate nursing curriculum. Collaborate with healthcare systems, behavioral health organizations, community agencies, and other clinical partners to provide high-quality learning experiences. Demonstrate a commitment to student success through teaching, advising, mentoring, and academic support. Maintain an active research and scholarly agenda. Demonstrate continuing scholarly growth compatible with the teacher-scholar model. Serve the School of Nursing, College of Health Sciences, University, profession, and community through participation in committees and other service activities. Advise and mentor students. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Nursing or a closely related field Evidence of matriculation and significant progress in a doctoral program of study, with the expectation that the terminal degree will be completed by the end of the second year of appointment Eligibility for Registered Nurse licensure in Pennsylvania, with verification of licensure required at the start of employment At least two years of professional nursing experience in psychiatric-mental health and/or behavioral health nursing practice Ability to meet the requirements of contractual affiliation agreements with clinical partners. These requirements may include, but are not limited to, health requirements, physical guidelines, clinical hours, background clearances, and codes of conduct. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate in nursing or a closely related field; and/or Didactic teaching experience; and/or Experience teaching undergraduate psychiatric-mental health nursing courses or curriculum. Recent (within the last 5 years) clinical experience in psychiatric-mental health or behavioral health nursing. Experience teaching undergraduate prelicensure nursing students; and/or Experience with psychiatric-mental health simulation, standardized patients, therapeutic communication activities, or other innovative experiential learning strategies; and/or Experience providing behavioral health services to a diverse population across multiple settings; and/or Experience using learning management systems such as D2L, Canvas, Blackboard, or similar platforms. This includes using the educational technology in mixed modalities (face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online); and/or Evidence of scholarly activity and/or potential for development of a sustained program of scholarship; and/or Experience teaching, advising, or mentoring students from diverse backgrounds. Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, research presentation, and teaching demonstration to be considered as a finalist. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Unofficial transcript(s); official transcripts will be required for final consideration List of three (3) references. Provide name, email address, and phone number for each reference. Service Statement (see below): West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational 