    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5480006/27-34-tenure-track-assistant-associate-professor-of-nutrition": {
      "title": "27-34 Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Nutrition",
      "description": "27-34 Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Nutrition Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-34 Department College of Health Sciences Division Nutrition Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus community whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Department of Nutrition invites applicants for a Full-time, 9-month, Tenure-Track, Assistant/Associate Professor of Nutrition with a specialty in clinical nutrition. Appointment rank will be determined based on experience and expertise. The position begins in August 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The College of Health Sciences offers many graduate programs, including one of the University’s four doctoral degrees and a diverse range of master’s degrees and certificate options. The mission of the Department of Nutrition in the College of Health Sciences at West Chester University is to shape tomorrow’s nutrition and dietetics professionals and leaders through quality, relevant, and innovative teaching, service, and scholarship. The Nutrition Department offers degrees at the undergraduate and graduate levels; undergraduate Didactic Program in Dietetics (DPD) (accredited), Master of Science in Community Nutrition (MSCN), and Dietetic Internship (accredited). The degree and curriculum options offer a wide variety of rewarding career opportunities including clinical dietetics, community/public health nutrition, sports nutrition, wellness, foodservice management, and state of the art interprofessional and simulation opportunities. Learn more about the Department of Nutrition . The ideal candidate will share WCU’s demonstrated commitment to equity, diversity, and inclusion, have prior experience working with culturally and socio-economically diverse populations, and will contribute to student success through inclusive pedagogy, scholarship, and service to the University and surrounding West Chester University communities. The typical course load involves teaching four courses per semester. Assignments may include opportunities for teaching at off-campus sites and/or through distance learning. Responsibilites include : Teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses including, but not limited to, Nutrition Assessment, Medical Nutrition Therapy I and II, Sports Nutrition, Lifecycle Nutrition, and others. Contributing to the curriculum and curriculum development in the undergraduate and graduate/dietetic internship programs Conducting research and other types of scholarly activities compatible with the teacher-scholar model Directing student projects Mentoring and advising students Serving the University and the community through participation in various committees Administrative duties assigned as needed Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in Nutrition or a closely related field. (ABD and terminal degree completed by the end of first year of employment will be considered with a letter from the dissertation chair outlining timeline for completion). Registered Dietitian Nutritionist credential (RD or RDN) Work experience in clinical nutrition Didactic teaching experience Preferred Qualifications Board certified specialist (sports dietetic, obesity and weight management, renal, etc.); and/or Work experience in sports nutrition; and/or Teaching experience with learning management systems such as Blackboard, D2L or Canvas; and/or Teaching experience with adult learners and experience using distance education technology Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compliant with a pplicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, research presentation, and teaching demonstration to be considered as a finalist. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Curriculum vitae Letter of application detailing interest in the position, qualifications, teaching philosophy, professional goals, related work experience, and scholarly activities. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required for finalist. List of three (3) references. Provide name, email address, and phone number for each reference. Letters will be electronically solicited at a later date. Service Statement (see below). Will be requested at a later date : West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Do you have a Doctorate in Nutrition or a closely related field? (ABD and terminal degree completed by the end of first year of employment will be considered with a letter from the dissertation chair outlining timeline for completion). Yes No 02 Are you a Registered Dietitian Nutritionist credential (RD or RDN)? Yes No 03 Do you have work experience in clinical nutrition? Yes No 04 Did you review and submit the applicable Required Documents for Consideration? Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5480173/27-35-tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-nutrition-and-dietetic-internship-progr": {
      "title": "27-35 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Nutrition and Dietetic Internship Program Director",
      "description": "27-35 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Nutrition and Dietetic Internship Program Director Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-35 Department College of the Sciences & Mathematics Opening Date 09/11/2026 Description Benefits Questions Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus community whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Department of Nutrition invites applicants for a Full-time, 12-month, Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor of Nutrition and Dietetic Internship Program Director. The position begins in July 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The mission of West Chester University’s Dietetic Internship program is to prepare program graduates to be competent entry-level registered dietitian nutritionists through high-quality graduate level education, relevant and innovative supervised practice experiences, and collaborative leadership opportunities. The Nutrition Department offers a wide variety of rewarding career opportunities including clinical dietetics, community/public health nutrition, sports nutrition, wellness, food service management, and others. Our faculty teach in state-of-the-art classrooms and interprofessional culinary and simulation laboratories. Learn more about the Department of Nutrition . The faculty position involves serving as the Program Director for West Chester University’s accredited Dietetic Internship Program and supporting the teaching, service, and clinical education mission of the Department of Nutrition. The Program Director will provide leadership and oversight for the ongoing administration, assessment, and continuous improvement of the Dietetic Internship Program in accordance with University requirements and Accreditation Council for Education in Nutrition and Dietetics (ACEND) standards. The individual will work collaboratively with the department chair and graduate and undergraduate program directors to allow for student success in alignment with the faculty collective bargaining agreement for a 12-month appointment. Responsibilities include : Serve as department Dietetic Internship Director and fulfill responsibilities outlined by ACEND Accreditation Standards including securing supervised practice sites and maintaining accreditation documentation and reports. Lead recruitment, application review, interview, selection, and onboarding processes for incoming dietetic interns. Teach graduate level courses in the dietetic internship program. Additional courses within area of specialization may be assigned based on departmental needs. Develop, implement, evaluate, and revise policies and procedures to effectively manage the dietetic internship within ACEND standards. Contribute to the curriculum and curriculum development in the graduate/dietetic internship programs. Develop and coordinate marketing, outreach, and recruitment initiatives including open houses, informational sessions, and promotional activities. Conduct regular intern evaluations and competency assessments, providing timely coaching, mentoring, and performance feedback. Preside over the Internship Advisory Committee meeting and Intern Selection committee. Mentoring and advising students. Engage in scholarly activities such as research, presentations, and publications. Serve the University and the community through participation in various committees. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Nutrition or a closely related field Must be a Registered Dietitian with CDR and provide state of PA licensure Minimum of three years of professional experience post-dietetics credentialing Preferred Qualifications Doctorate in Nutrition or a closely related field; and/or Professional work experience in a supervised practice program; and/or Experience using learning management systems geared towards distance education; and/or Teaching experience at the college or university level; and/or Familiarity with the accreditation process of supervised practice programs in dietetics Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Compliant with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, research presentation, and teaching demonstration to be considered as a finalist. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Curriculum vitae Letter of application detailing interest in the position, qualifications, teaching philosophy, professional goals, related work experience, and scholarly activities. Unofficial undergraduate and graduate transcripts. Official transcripts will be required for finalist. List of three (3) references. Provide name, email address, and phone number for each reference. Letters will be electronically solicited at a later date. Service Statement (see below). Will be requested at a later date : West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Promotion up the ranks of the professoriate will require candidates to have earned a requisite doctoral degree. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. 01 Do you have a Master’s degree in Nutrition or a closely related field? Yes No 02 Are you a Registered Dietitian with CDR and provide state of PA licensure? Yes No 03 Do you have a minimum of three years of professional experience post-dietetics credentialing? Yes No 04 Did you review and submit the applicable Required Documents for Consideration? Yes No Required Question Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa/jobs/5480683/27-21-tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-studio-composition": {
      "title": "27-21 Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Studio Composition",
      "description": "27-21 Tenure Track Assistant Professor of Studio Composition Location West Chester University, PA Job Type Regular / Full-Time Job Number 27-21 Department School of Music Division Music History, Theory & Composition Opening Date 09/14/2026 Description Benefits Position Summary Join a vibrant equity-minded campus whose excellence is reflected in its community, cultural engagement, and student success. The Department of Music Theory, History & Composition invites applicants for a full-time, tenure track, Assistant Professor of Studio Composition. The position begins in August 2027. West Chester University (WCU), a member of the Pennsylvania State System of Higher Education, is a public, comprehensive institution committed to offering high-quality undergraduate education, selected post-baccalaureate and graduate programs, and a variety of educational and cultural resources for its students, alumni, and citizens of southeastern Pennsylvania. The University offers more than 100 graduate and undergraduate programs in the sciences and mathematics, business and public management, arts and humanities, health sciences, education and social work, music, and interdisciplinary studies. We are a community of educators dedicated to developing graduates who succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good . The mission of the Department of Music Theory, History & Composition, part of the Wells School of Music, is to deliver an inclusive, world-class education that equips music majors with foundational strength in music theory, aural skills, history, and technology, while enriching non-majors and Music Production minors through accessible general education classes, performance opportunities, and practical experience in recording, composition, and music technology. Majors in Composition and Studio Composition receive robust instruction in the specializations of their fields and have ample opportunities for collaboration, recording, and ensemble participation. The Wells School of Music serves approximately 450 students with 60 faculty and enjoys full NASM membership. Review additional information about West Chester University’s Studio Composition Degree. The faculty position involves teaching undergraduate and/or graduate level courses that will focus on in-person instruction with the possibility of online and/or hybrid modalities depending on departmental needs. The ideal candidate will use innovative teaching skills and demonstrate strong attention to the learning and teaching needs of the department’s students. Their experience, substantive specialization, and pedagogical training will serve to strengthen the department's mission and vision. The faculty will collaborate with other departmental and college faculty & staff to ensure student success. The typical course load involves teaching 12 credits per semester. Responsibilities include: Teach courses including Scoring for Film and Media, Scoring Video Games, and Senior Projects in Studio Composition Collaborate with Department and Wells School of Music faculty on program evaluation, governance, recruitment, student advising, and daily operations Additional responsibilities may include: Oversee the Center for Music Technology, lead the Studio Music Ensemble, and teach related courses (such as Studio Production, Computer Music, Music Entrepreneurship, and Songwriting). Other courses may be assigned based on area of specialization depending on department needs. Advise students majoring in Studio Composition and minoring in Music Production Maintain activity in creative, commercial, and/or scholarly endeavors Serve the Department and University community through participation in various committees Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications A Master’s degree in Music or a closely related field completed before August 2027 Demonstrated record of active achievement in scoring for film, media, and /or video games Demonstrated experience in recording techniques and studio production Demonstrated experience teaching at the college level Preferred Qualifications A Doctoral degree in Music or a closely related field; and/or Demonstrated ability to develop innovative curriculum Special Instructions West Chester University of Pennsylvania offers highly competitive salaries and excellent benefits . Apply online at https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/wcupa . Incomplete applications will not be reviewed. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. In accordance with applicable collective bargaining agreement, this advertisement may be closed without notice upon receipt of a sufficient pool of qualified candidates. Applicants must successfully complete the application, interview process, teaching demonstration, and research presentation to be considered a finalist. Required Documents for Consideration To be considered as an applicant for this position, in addition to the application form, please submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae List of three (3) references (Include name, email address, and phone number for each reference). Letters of recommendation will be solicited electronically from the references at a later date. At a later date, the following with be requested: Statement of teaching philosophy A portfolio that includes creative/commercial work samples Service Statement (See below): West Chester University is a community of educators that develops graduates to succeed personally and professionally and contribute to the common good. WCU GRADUATES WILL: Apply scientific reasoning and demonstrate quantitative and qualitative literacy Collaborate with others to solve problems and address societal needs Communicate effectively and participate in civic discourse Engage inclusively in a diverse society Understand the ethical implications of decisions and the world in which they live INSTITUTIONAL GOALS: To fulfill its mission as a public institution serving the Commonwealth, West Chester University will focus on student success and institutional improvement as measured by the degree to which WCU demonstrates: Access to learning Community and cultural engagement Continuous improvement Critical thinking Inclusion Scholarly and creative activities Sustainability Given this, please select from one of the prompts below to create a service statement (no more than 1 page) Engagement with the Campus Community Describe your efforts to create an inclusive and supportive campus environment for all students, faculty, and staff. How have you contributed to fostering a sense of belonging in your department or institution? Mentorship and Student Support How have you worked to support and mentor students with a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives? Share specific examples of how you have helped students navigate challenges in their academic or professional journeys. Outreach and Community Involvement Discuss your experiences working with community organizations, schools, or educational programs that aim to expand access to higher education. How have you helped ensure broader participation in your field? Pedagogical and Curricular Contributions How have you contributed to developing curricula, programs, or initiatives that are accessible and relevant to a broad range of students? Provide examples of how you have designed or implemented courses that engage with multiple perspectives. Professional Development and Collaboration Reflect on your participation in initiatives, committees, or professional development activities that aim to create a welcoming academic environment. How have you collaborated with colleagues to enhance student success and engagement? Research and Scholarship Impact In what ways has your research or scholarly work contributed to increasing opportunities, perspectives, and voices in your field? Describe any projects or initiatives aimed at broadening participation, access or engagement. All offers of employment are subject to and contingent upon satisfactory completion of all preemployment criminal background checks. Developing and sustaining a diverse faculty and staff advances West Chester University’s educational mission. West Chester University is an Affirmative Action – Equal Opportunity Employer. CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act and Act 73 of 1988, West Chester University publishes a combined Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR). The ASFSR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASFSR is available for review on the Public Safety website . Application Questions? Email hrs@wcupa.edu for questions regarding the application process. WCU proudly offers comprehensive employee benefits including health, vision, and dental insurance, generous retirement plans, many wellness programs, a tuition waiver for self and family members, and training, development and advancement opportunities. On the first working day, new employees are eligible to enroll in medical, prescription, dental and vision benefit plans. Medical and prescription drug coverage includes PPO health, prescription drug, and hearing coverage. Dental and vision coverage is offered at no cost to employees. The Healthy U Wellness program rewards participants with reduced health care premiums and provides tools and resources to maintain good health. Flexible spending accounts allow employees to withhold income from their paychecks before taxes for reimbursement of approved medical and dependent care expenses. A University mission to support employee personal and professional growth. PASSHE tuition waiver lowers the cost of college expenses. Leave and time-off benefits include generous paid vacation, paid sick time, military leave and paid time off for most major holidays. Choice of two group retirement plans with generous employer contributions. Voluntary retirement plans offer two additional options to save and invest money for retirement and are available to all employees upon their date of hire. Group life insurance is provided at no cost to all permanent employees. Voluntary long-term disability insurance (LTD) and voluntary group life and personal accident insurance (VGLIP/AD&D) are available to employees. State Employee Assistance Program (SEAP) provides a wide range of free services including counseling, legal, and financial services. The employee group for this position is Association of Pennsylvania State College and University Faculties (APSCUF). For additional benefit details please see the PASSHE EMPLOYEE BENEFITS PAGE . The information is provided for general purposes only. Legal Plan Documents will govern any discrepancies that may arise. Benefits, benefit levels, and eligibility rules are subject to change. The benefits described are available to most employees; however, certain eligibility requirements must be met. Employer West Chester University Address 201 Carter Drive, Suite 100 West Chester, Pennsylvania, 19383 Website http://www.wcupa.edu Apply"
